<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Sacred Heart College Portfolio - Profile</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Top Header Title Area -->
    <header class="site-header">
        <div class="header-container">
            <span class="school-title">SACRED HEART</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Official Navy Blue Navigation Bar -->
    <nav class="main-nav">
        <a href="/" class="nav-link active">Profile</a>
        <a href="/pillar-one" class="nav-link">1st Pillar</a>
        <a href="/pillar-two" class="nav-link">2nd Pillar</a>
    </nav>

    <!-- Main Content Canvas (Sky Blue) -->
    <main class="content-wrapper">
        <div class="page-container">
            
            <h1>Profile</h1>
            
            <!-- Profile Image Setup -->
            <div class="profile-image-container">
                <img src="/images/Keane me .png" alt="Keane's Portrait" class="profile-photo">
            </div>

            <!-- About Me Bio Section -->
            <section class="bio-section">
                <h2>Welcome to My Website</h2>
                <p>My name is Keane and I am a Year 10 student at Sacred Heart College. I have arrived in Sacred Heart College last year. The activities and subjects I have done in school gave me a great opportunity to get more comfortable in school. 
                This Website will have 2 Pillars that I relate most at school and at home. 
                 </p>
            </section>

            <!-- Hobbies & Interests Section -->
            <section class="interests-section">
                <h2>Interests & Hobbies</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>I like playing sports such as football, basketball and badminton</li>
                    <li>My hobbies are building with lego and playing video games</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

        </div>
    </main>

</body>
</html>
